APPENDIX A — Plain Language

How do tiles talk to each other?
Through a message, not shared memory.
Can any tile call any other tile?
No. Only the calls that were burned into ROM are allowed.
Can tile A call tile B, and B call A?
No. The call graph is a one-way street. No loops.
How deep can the calls go?
Three levels. No more.
What does the caller send?
A task, a budget, and a hash of the state the callee is allowed to see.
What does the callee send back?
The result, its signature, and how many cycles it used.
Are both tiles ever on at the same time?
No. The caller goes dark, the callee wakes up, they swap back.
Why?
Because isolation is what makes the system certifiable.
What is this called?
A6 — the tile invocation protocol.

